# Mobile (iOS / Android)

The same codebase — React frontend, Rust commands, state, events — also builds
native mobile apps. `lib.rs` carries the mobile entry point
(`#[cfg_attr(mobile, tauri::mobile_entry_point)]`, rule BE012), so no code
changes are needed to go mobile.

## Prerequisites

Run `dude doctor` — the "(mobile)" rows tell you what is missing.

- **Android** (any OS): Android Studio with SDK + NDK, `ANDROID_HOME` and
  `NDK_HOME` exported, a Java runtime. See the
  [Tauri prerequisites](https://tauri.app/start/prerequisites/#android).
- **iOS** (macOS only): full Xcode (the Command Line Tools alone are not
  enough) and CocoaPods (`brew install cocoapods`).

The Rust cross-compilation targets are installed automatically by
`dude android init` / `dude ios init`.

## One-time setup per platform

```bash
dude android init   # generates src-tauri/gen/android + installs Rust targets
dude ios init       # generates src-tauri/gen/apple  + installs Rust targets
```

Both commands also refresh the app icons into the generated native project
(from `app-icon.png`). **Commit `src-tauri/gen/`** — the native projects are
scaffolded once and version-controlled; you edit them for native-level
customisation (permissions in `AndroidManifest.xml`, `Info.plist`, signing).

## Development

```bash
dude android dev            # emulator (or Android Studio via --open)
dude ios dev                # simulator (or Xcode via --open)

dude android dev --host     # physical device on the same network
dude ios dev --host
```

`--host` exposes the Vite dev server on your LAN IP (wired through
`TAURI_DEV_HOST` in `vite.config.ts`) so the device can reach it. Hot-reload
works on device.

## Release builds

```bash
dude android build --aab                  # Play Store bundle
dude android build --apk --target aarch64 # sideloadable APK, one ABI
dude ios build                            # IPA (App Store Connect export)
dude ios build --export-method debugging  # ad-hoc/dev IPA
```

Signing is configured in the native projects: keystore setup for Android in
`src-tauri/gen/android`, certificates/profiles for iOS via Xcode in
`src-tauri/gen/apple`. See the
[Tauri distribution guide](https://tauri.app/distribute/) for store-specific
steps.

## Caveats

- The `identifier` in `tauri.conf.json` must stay alphanumeric-dot-separated
  (rule BE009): Android forbids dashes, Apple forbids underscores.
- Plugin support differs per platform — check each plugin's platform table
  before relying on it in mobile builds (log and opener both support mobile).
- The window size settings in `tauri.conf.json` are ignored on mobile; the
  webview fills the screen. Test responsive layouts (the antd grid used on the
  Home page already adapts).
